> I like this use of "gi" because connected lists are by far more common=20
> than embedded binary connectives. The meanings of "ge ... gi ... gi ..."=
=20
> and "ga ... gi ... gi ..." are fairly obvious, but what are the proposed=
=20
> generalizations for "go" and "gu"? Is "go" all true or all false? What ar=
