La zantufa gives only syntactic structure, and I have not yet suggested the=
=20
semantic structure. From any approach, it is reasonable to interpret that=
=20
{gu A gi B gi C} has the same truth value as A.

As for {se gu}, one of possible interpretations is grouping of binary=20
transitive connective: that is, {segu A gi B gi C} =3D {segu (segu A gi B=
=20
gi'i) gi C} =3D {segu A gi (segu B gi C)}, and then the truth value of {seg=
u=20
A gi B gi C} is the same as C. However, as you suggested, we may give=20
another interpretation that {se gu} draws the truth value of B, {te gu}=20
draws the truth value of C, and so on. I like the latter interpretation,=20
because it cannot be easily represented by grouping system of binary=20
connectives, and therefore profits from the n-ary forethought connective=20
system.

For the same reason, I prefer the interpretation of "all true or all false"=
=20
for {go} and "one and only one of them is true" for {gonai} to the=20
interpretation of grouping of binary connectives.
=20

